# Personal Configuration (example)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` and edit it with your own habits, workout rotation, and
preferences:

```bash
cp CLAUDE.local.md.example CLAUDE.local.md
```

`CLAUDE.local.md` is gitignored and auto-loaded by Claude Code alongside `CLAUDE.md`, so
your personal setup stays private and local while the generic rules in `CLAUDE.md` stay
shared. If `CLAUDE.local.md` is absent, nothing breaks — you just lose the personalization.

The sections below are the maintainer's real configuration, kept as a worked example.

## My habits

- Casual name → actual habit mappings: "lifting" → Weights Workout, "ran" → Run 10k,
  "meditated" → Complete Meditation.
- Multi-rep habits: meditation has a daily goal of 2. "Log a meditation" = 1 rep (not the
  whole habit).
- "Full meditation" / "complete meditation" = one proper (not short) session — "full" refers
  to the quality of the session, NOT the quantity. Log as 1 rep unless I explicitly say I did
  both (e.g. "did both meditations").
- When a workout includes pull-ups (part of a Pull/Back session), also tick my pull-up habit.

## My workout rotation

- Strict order: **Pull → Push → Leg → Pull → Push → Leg**. After a Pull the next is ALWAYS
  Push; after Push ALWAYS Leg; after Leg ALWAYS Pull. Rest days don't reset the order — just
  resume where I left off. Check my last workout type and give the next in sequence.
- Back-day variant: an alternate Pull workout with more isolation / cable work. It counts as
  the Pull slot in the rotation.

## My diet & food preferences

- Vegetarian. No egg, fish, onion, garlic, mushroom, or leek.
- Be conservative with protein/calorie estimates when logging nutrition.
- Apply these when logging meals or suggesting food.
